1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Automatic window display

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
The window display is the basis for automatic window display function.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Move the mouse to the 3D window to display the virtual model.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Click to display the virtual model window display.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,000
You can see that the virtual model's body surface is covered with a layer of natural invisible clothing.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
It will not directly affect the clothing you make,

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
but through the model body data contained in it,

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
it can help you quickly adjust the size of the clothing to adapt to multiple virtual models of different bodies.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
The virtual model worn by Marvelous Designer is worn with a window display.

10
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:43,000
If the virtual model you import from the outside does not have window display information,

11
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:47,000
you can automatically create a window display when you import it.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,000
When the standard A-Pose or T-Pose model is imported to Marvelous Designer,

13
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
it can automatically generate window display information.

14
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,000
If you want to create a window display,

15
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
you may not be satisfied with the effect of the window display.

16
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Or sometimes,

17
00:00:58,000 --> 00:00:59,000
because the pose is special,

18
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:03,000
or the human body recognition is accurate when A-Pose or T-Pose is used,

19
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
it may fail to create a window display.

20
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
At this time, you need to define and edit your window display.

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Click on the virtual model image in the menu bar.

22
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Click on the virtual model editor.

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Then switch to the window display label page.

24
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
You can see that there are some purple measurement lines on the model body.

25
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
In contrast to the visual image,

26
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
check if there are purple measurement lines that are not perfectly identified or cannot be identified.

27
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
You can click on the name of the part that needs to be modified.

28
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Add a purple measurement line to the model body.

29
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,000
The original measurement line on the part will be replaced with the measurement line you have defined.

30
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
After the check is complete, click on the window display.

31
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
The model body is covered with a layer of window display.

32
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
If there is a gap between the window screen and the model body,

33
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,000
you can pull it out a little bit.

34
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:06,000
The model body and the model are translated into .apt.

35
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Next time, you can directly call the model that contains the window display information.

36
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:18,000
The window display information will also be stored on the clothing.

37
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Open the clothing window display.

38
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
You can see that the clothing is also covered with a red window display.

39
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
You can see that the clothing is also covered with a red window display.

40
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Press Shift A to display the virtual model Hanna that we have already opened in advance.

41
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Let's try the virtual model function in the 3D window.

42
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
You can see that the clothes are worn on the virtual model.

43
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:43,000
But this function will not automatically adjust the clothes to fit the model.

44
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,000
It just automatically wears the clothes.

45
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
So the clothes may look too tight or loose.

46
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Press Alt-6 to check the hard drive.

47
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
You can see that the clothes are too loose.

48
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Press G to return to the previous step.

49
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
You can increase the particle diameter of the clothes before computing.

50
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
You can make the calculation speed faster.

51
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:06,000
This time, we try to operate the automatic adjustment of the panel in the 2D window.

52
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Press C to select these functions.

53
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
You can see that the panel has been changed.

54
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The clothing line is now more in harmony with the virtual model.

55
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:17,000
We will see you next time.

56
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Thank you for watching.

